vement/a-79753482?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In a seismic political shift, Serbia's longtime strongman leader Aleksandar Vucic has conceded defeat to a student-led movement in the country's parliamentary elections.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Protein shakes for teenagers: Good or bad idea?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad9bcfb59d5036d4697affd7445dc044501926b7b4964f9b52ebc2ce2a9721f8</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T16:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/protein-shakes-for-teenagers-good-or-bad-idea/a-79751929--869a08ab5ad1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/protein-shakes-for-teenagers-good-or-bad-idea/a-79751929?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Protein products are marketed as a way of building muscle and losing weight — and they're very popular with young people. They also claim to promote healthy growth in children. Is this true? How much protein is healthy?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda says it has no active Ebola cases, but infections in Kenya and Nigeria are prompting fresh scrutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85b05148fe9d66fcec28e83974135e2866e5a53849f839c31ffd863a6644152a</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T13:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-says-it-has-no-active-ebola-cases-but-infections-in-kenya-and-nigeria-are-prompting-fresh-scr/a-79741580--819bf739b307.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-says-it-has-no-active-ebola-cases-but-infections-in-kenya-and-nigeria-are-prompting-fresh-scrutiny/a-79741580?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Health officials are investigating whether Ebola patients in Kenya and Nigeria crossed paths at Uganda's main airport as conflicting accounts cloud the source of one infection.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Harry Kane: Ballon d’Or for Bayern Munich striker?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4178a155c407ed7820c4ffa6c0dcdc47b65e4a9b251f9980ad7b611ebf296b80</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T13:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299--2a5c9f9ed870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich striker Harry Kane is the clear front-runner for football's most prestigious individual prize, which will be awarded on Monday. Kane has developed even more in the Bundesliga despite an uneven league.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Israel to close all West Bank land crossings on election day</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5cfdcc3da8d704567a10a821362c42b0761c59633f26fdb1e7bd92e67c81bde</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T13:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-to-close-all-west-bank-land-crossings-on-election-day/a-79755010--68b876b070e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-to-close-all-west-bank-land-crossings-on-election-day/a-79755010?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a deadly attack which killed two Israeli soldiers on Friday, the Israeli military has said all land border points between Israel and the occupied West Bank will be closed during Tuesday's election.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Fire flares up at Hitler's Eagle's Nest retreat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66619d770c73b27e4c5a057d6655368305a780241fd1f747b0580723c03db210</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T12:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-fire-flares-up-at-hitler-s-eagle-s-nest-retreat/live-79749353--9bb59e2ba8a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-fire-flares-up-at-hitler-s-eagle-s-nest-retreat/live-79749353?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fire broke out again overnight at a former mountain retreat used by Nazi dictator Adolf Hitler. Meanwhile, a survey shows most people in Germany feel the days of the governing coalition are numbered.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France: Hundreds arrested after nationwide protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:490190885b2485618a0dec41908dc7b504af1fde4dd371744d386209114b8ef0</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T12:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-protests-more-violence-feared-amid-renewed-demonstrations/live-79748223--43db314a2270.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-hundreds-arrested-after-nationwide-protests/live-79748223?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The French government says more than 1,000 people were arrested following nationwide protests on Saturday. Police and elite security forces were out in force across the country as clashes broke out.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil votes in tight runoff between leftist Lula and right-wing Flavio Bolsonaro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ae6d04a028d5f8c43de7a0aa06b26393e6257b3ee78c8b0db6959d98358fa59</id><updated>2026-10-26T05:00:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T11:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-votes-in-tight-runoff-between-leftist-lula-and-right-wing-flavio-bolsonaro/a-79753924--f6f7682c4c53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-votes-in-tight-runoff-between-leftist-lula-and-right-wing-flavio-bolsonaro/a-79753924?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xm